{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Find flights{% endblock %}

{% block description %}Search one-way and return flights, with the cheapest fare marked on every day of the calendar and dates you can flex by up to three days.{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
{# The landmark this page did not have, around the whole block rather than
   around part of it -- and that is a constraint, not a preference.

   `.hero__bar` is `position: sticky` above 768px, and a sticky element is
   measured against its containing block. `.page` is what bounds it today, and
   layout.html.twig's own note records what happens without a bound: the bar
   "stayed pinned over the footer". Wrapping everything makes this box exactly
   `.page`'s, so the bar's travel is unchanged. Wrapping any subset of the five
   bands would move that boundary, silently, and only once somebody scrolled.

   The bands stay siblings of each other, so `.hero-cards`' negative top margin
   still straddles `.hero__tail` the way it did. #}
<main role="main">
{# The hero is a flat band, not a photograph.

   It used to be one of ten background JPEGs picked at random per request, with
   the form squeezed into five columns on top of it. That gave the page no
   stable identity -- every visit looked like a different site -- put a large
   image request above the fold, and left white text sitting on whatever the
   photo happened to be behind it. A flat field means the white search bar is
   the brightest thing on the screen, which is where the visitor is meant to
   look. The photography moves down to the destination cards, where an image is
   the content rather than a backdrop. #}
<div class="hero">
    <div class="container hero__inner">
        <h1 class="hero__slogan">Build the trip, not&nbsp;just the ticket</h1>

        {# The tray at rest. global.js lifts it into the header once it has
           gone under, and puts it back on the way up. #}
        <div class="hero__modes-slot js-modes-slot">
            {% include 'partials/sections.html.twig' only %}

        {# The line the tray crosses on the way out.

           At the foot of the slot, not the head of it: the tray moves up to the
           header only once it has gone under it completely, and it is the
           bottom edge that says when that is. Put above, it docked while the
           tray was still half in view and two copies of the same thing appeared
           to be on screen at once.

           Inside the slot rather than on the tray, because the tray is lifted
           away and something that has moved can no longer say where it used to
           be. The slot keeps its height while the tray is gone, so this stays
           where it is. #}
        <div class="hero__modes-sentinel js-modes-sentinel" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        </div>

    </div>
</div>

{# The search bar, and the band it sits in.

   Its own block rather than part of the hero above, which is what lets it be
   `position: sticky`. Sticky is bounded by its parent, and inside the hero it
   would have come unstuck the moment the hero ended; as a child of the body it
   is bounded by the page. That is worth the extra element, because the
   alternative -- pinning it from JS -- cannot be made not to jump: a scroll runs
   on the compositor and a scroll handler runs on the main thread, so on a flick
   the page has already moved by the time the class lands, and the bar arrives
   where the scroll got to and drops into place. Sticky is handled where the
   scrolling is, and never lags it.

   The band is the hero's own colour, so at rest this reads as the foot of the
   hero rather than as a strip of its own.

   The whole form lives in search/form.html.twig. The hero used to carry its own
   copy: a Round trip tab that shipped `disabled`, a cabin select comparing
   'economy' to itself so it always rendered Economy, and the passenger partial
   included with no party so it always said one adult. #}
<div class="hero__bar js-hero-bar">
    <div class="container">
        {% include 'search/form.html.twig' with {
            'places': places,
            'recent': recent,
            'depart_date': today_date
        } only %}
    </div>
</div>

{# The rest of the band's depth, below the bar. It cannot be padding on the bar,
   which would make the sticky strip that tall and pin a band most of a screen
   deep; and it cannot be padding on the hero, which stops above the bar. #}
<div class="hero__tail" aria-hidden="true"></div>

{# Lifted into the band so the cards straddle its edge, the way the reference
   does. They stay where they were in the document -- the overlap is a margin,
   not a position -- so the reading order is still hero, then destinations. #}
<div class="container hero-cards">
    <div class="row row-cols-1 row-cols-lg-3 align-items-stretch g-4">
        {% for poi in poi_cards %}
            {% include 'index/poi.html.twig' %}
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
</div>

<div class="container px-4 py-5" id="icon-grid">
    <h2 class="pb-2 mb-4 border-bottom">Top searches</h2>

    <div class="list-group">
        {% for search in top_searches %}
            {% include 'index/top-search.html.twig' with {'rank': loop.index} %}
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
</div>
</main>
{% endblock %}
